<title>SPAIN: Spain's Endesa/CNMV suit could end soon - press.</title>
<headline>Spain's Endesa/CNMV suit could end soon - press.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Spanish Stock market Commission's (CNMV) suit against the electricity firm Endesa could end very soon, a local agency reported on Monday.</p>
<p>On December 18, the CNMV filed a suit for a &quot;very serious infraction&quot; against the state electricity firm for failing to inform the authority in October of its plans to buy Sevillana and Fecsa.</p>
<p>At the time, the commission proposed fines of up to 48 billion pesetas.</p>
<p>The CNMV also filed suit against Endesa's ex-chairman Feliciano Fuster and its finance director, proposing fines of up to fifty million pesetas each.</p>
<p>Earlier this month, Spanish state holding company SEPI replaced Endesa's Feliciano Fuster with Rodolfo Martin Villa.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
</text>
